Subject: [SE4-P2] winedmo: decouple the descriptor's stream selection from active streams

GE-Proton11-12's Wine bump made media_source_CreatePresentationDescriptor()
select only the streams that are active, so that a descriptor created after
Start reports the selection that was started. In the base, streams are
created active, so the default descriptor still selects every stream.
0002 creates streams inactive, because the demux thread idles until a
stream is active, and its Stop deactivates them. Together, a descriptor
created before the first Start, or after Stop, selected nothing: MFPlay's
SetMediaItem failed with E_INVALIDARG, and a SourceReader client that
reads without SetStreamSelection() had its reads refused.

Track the reported selection in its own field: every stream until the
first Start, then the streams of the last committed Start. Stop, a failed
seek and Shutdown leave it alone, as the base and Wine's mfsrcsnk source
leave their selection on Stop. 'active' and all of its readers are
unchanged.

Compile-checked only (x86_64 and i386, the SE4-P1 build's per-file commands,
-Werror); not runtime-qualified.

---
diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c b/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c
@@ -284,6 +284,9 @@
 
     DWORD stream_id;
     BOOL active;
+    /* Selection reported by CreatePresentationDescriptor, under source->cs:
+     * every stream until the first Start, then the last committed Start. */
+    BOOL selected;
     BOOL paused;
     BOOL eos;
     LONG eos_epoch;
@@ -1428,6 +1431,7 @@
         if (was_active && !descriptors[i])
             ++stream->request_generation;
         stream->active = !!descriptors[i];
+        stream->selected = stream->active;
         if (!stream->active)
         {
             media_packet_queue_flush(stream);
@@ -2351,6 +2355,7 @@
     object->descriptor = descriptor;
 
     object->active = FALSE;
+    object->selected = TRUE;
     object->eos = FALSE;
     object->stream_index = stream_index;
     object->is_video = is_video;
@@ -2849,9 +2854,11 @@
                 (const BYTE *)&source->origin, sizeof(source->origin))))
             WARN("Failed to set presentation origin, hr %#lx.\n", hr);
 
+        /* Not 'active': streams stay inactive until Start so that the demux
+         * thread idles, and Stop or a failed seek deactivates them. */
         for (i = 0; i < source->stream_count; ++i)
         {
-            if (!source->streams[i]->active)
+            if (!source->streams[i]->selected)
                 continue;
 
             if (FAILED(hr = IMFPresentationDescriptor_SelectStream(*descriptor, i)))
